-- @DESC: Lambda inline — an anonymous lambda is called immediately with arguments, spec/07 §2.2
-- @AI: No - self-sufficient: assertion-only, no stdout.
-- @DISABLED: Lambda-as-processing-argument is unimplemented: invoking an anonymous lambda immediately `((x,y) => x+y)(...)` and passing a lambda as a rule argument are both E0009 syntax errors (spec/07 §2.2 deferred).
rule main:
  new result := λ((x, y) => x + y)(10, 20);
  expect result = 30;
return;
